# --- Splitz Specific ---
# Agent tooling and skill installs are per-developer, not project config.
# `.agents/` already covers the skills; skills-lock.json pins local copies to
# upstream and has no meaning to anyone else. Both were tracked by accident.
.agents/
skills-lock.json
.gemini/
conductor/
test-results/
ci-lint.log
ci-compile.log
ci-test.log
progress.txt
ralph_prompt.md

# --- Spring Boot ---
# Only ignore local/secret properties, keep base ones.
# src/main/resources/application.properties is tracked: it holds no secrets (every
# sensitive value reads from an env var with a dev default) and CI needs it, since
# the e2e job boots the services straight from a checkout.
**/application-local.properties
**/application-dev-local.properties
**/application-prod-local.properties
